part prices
  tally 1
  note "Fund prices. History: the market files' rows that a question reads, each in a version known on its valuation day and citing its file and line (the files are not imported whole; the Wektor files' decimal comma and day-first dates are a dialect, O:A-1)."
  note "Forecast (A-12): each fund's price moves on each month's last day by the path's rate and is then rounded to the places its fund quotes in (story § The forecast, item 3). Those rules point at the version fc_moves of the scenario forecast (scenarios/forecast.tally), so outside it they are never candidates (L §6.4)."
  note "px_round: the story doesn't say how a moved price is rounded to its places (L §7.2: an unstated mode is an axis)."
  note "Item 4 keeps Ania's units and the workplace plans outside the forecast, yet item 3 moves every fund's price and item 5 sells both Rzeka accounts, Ania's 4471-07 included: the text moves every price but WEK-WCP-2055's (case suspect, A-12)."

axis px_round
  nearest "a moved price is rounded to its fund's places, half up"
  cut "a moved price is cut to its fund's places"

input path_rate[m in month]: num question "By what rate does every fund's price move on this month's last day (story § The forecast, item 3)?"

input fc_base: month question "From which month's last price does the forecast move prices?"

input mk_glb[d in day]: num DUK/fund_u question "What is BRZ-GLB-A's price on this valuation day (brz-glb-a.csv)?"

version mk_glb_20230912
  cite market
  known 2023-09-12
  mk_glb[2023-09-12] = 176.40 "brz-glb-a.csv line 1447"

version mk_glb_20240307
  cite market
  known 2024-03-07
  mk_glb[2024-03-07] = 187.59 "brz-glb-a.csv line 1570"

version mk_glb_20251231
  cite market
  known 2025-12-31
  mk_glb[2025-12-31] = 230.56 "brz-glb-a.csv line 2027"

def pm_glb[m in month]: num DUK/fund_u
  note "BRZ-GLB-A's price at the end of month m: the market row, then, in the forecast, the path's move rounded to the fund's places"
  rule market_end = mk_glb[add_days(end_of(m), -1)]
  rule nearest excepts market_end v fc_moves when pos(m) > 1 and m > fc_base and px_round = nearest = round(pm_glb[m - 1] * (1 + path_rate[m]), 0.01, half-up)
  rule cut excepts market_end v fc_moves when pos(m) > 1 and m > fc_base and px_round = cut = round(pm_glb[m - 1] * (1 + path_rate[m]), 0.01, down)

def px_glb[d in day]: num DUK/fund_u
  note "BRZ-GLB-A's price on day d: the market row; in the forecast, the last month-end price on or before d"
  rule market = mk_glb[d]
  rule forecast excepts market v fc_moves when month_of(d) > fc_base = (if d = add_days(end_of(month_of(d)), -1) then pm_glb[month_of(d)] else pm_glb[month_of(d) - 1])

